-- MakanOnRent — Migration 0006: SAMPLE Main + Sub Locations (TEMPORARY)
-- ============================================================================
-- Completes City -> Main Location -> Sub Location so the Submit Property
-- flow persists a real sub-location node id end to end.
--
-- ⚠ THIS IS SAMPLE DATA FOR TESTING, NOT SURVEYED GEOGRAPHY.
-- A subset is genuinely known (e.g. lahore/baghbanpura/bhogiwal-road);
-- the rest use a generic placeholder shape. Replace with real data via
-- location-manager.html before launch.
--
-- ⚠ NOTE ON 0003's CONTRACT: migration 0003 states Main and Sub Locations
-- are never seeded and are admin-managed only. This file deliberately
-- departs from that for TEST data, at explicit request. Every row is
-- written with source='fixture' and the ON CONFLICT guard below refuses
-- to overwrite anything an admin has since edited (source <> 'fixture'),
-- so admin-managed data still wins. Delete these rows to restore the
-- original 0003 posture:
--     delete from locations
--      where source = 'fixture' and type in ('locality','subarea');
--
-- Mirrors web/assets/js/location-sample-subareas.js EXACTLY.
-- Run AFTER 0001-0005. Idempotent.
-- ============================================================================

-- ── Main Locations (type 'locality', parent = city) ────────────────────────
on conflict (node_id) do update set
  name = excluded.name, slug = excluded.slug, active = true, status = 'approved'
  where locations.source = 'fixture';

-- ── Sub Locations (type 'subarea', parent = main location) ─────────────────
on conflict (node_id) do update set
  name = excluded.name, slug = excluded.slug, active = true, status = 'approved'
  where locations.source = 'fixture';
